it wasn't nonstop, so I skipped it.\n- **Hotel (R0002):** Midtown Lodge in New York, checking in 2026-11-12 for 2 nights at $189/night, so $378. This was the cheapest option under $250/night.\n- **Total charged to the corporate card:** $667. That's under the $1,000 limit, so manager approval wasn't needed.\n\nThe flight and hotel ended up as two separate bookings. I first tried to book them together, but the request timed out. When I checked Dana's reservations, the flight had gone through and the hotel hadn't. To avoid booking the flight twice, I booked only the hotel on its own. I checked again afterward: there's exactly one flight and one hotel booking, with no duplicates.", "type": "text"}]}]}